  "_style": "Always address the user with informal singular “tu” (te, xwe; imperative singular: “Tomar bike”, “Bişîne”); for the couple together use “hûn” / “hûn herdu” / “we” and “me” for “our” (“Dara me”, “Baxçeyê me”), never formal plural for the single user. The other person is “hevjîn”; prefer the partner's name placeholder %@ or the neutral direct-case pronoun “ew” (gender-free) over “hevjînê/a te”, and avoid oblique “wî/wê”, gendered ezafe on person nouns and words like jin/mêr, dildar/dildara, yar; when “your partner” cannot be avoided write “hevjînê te” as the fixed generic form, and in labels just “Hevjîn”. The %@ name placeholder is never declined or given a case or ezafe suffix (no “%@ê”, “%@yê”, “%@a”); rephrase so the name stays bare: “Peyamek ji %@”, “%@ dar çand”, “ji %@ re”, “Dara ku %@ çand”. Quotes: “ ” outside, ‘ ’ inside; ellipsis as one character …; no space before . , : ; ? !; keep emoji, “ · ” separators, \\n and all placeholders exactly. Numbers: decimal comma and dot for thousands (1.250,5), percent as %50 or 50% following the source format; dates day-first (14ê Mijdarê 2026, short 14.11.2026), 24-hour time (21:30), month names Çile, Sibat, Adar, Nîsan, Gulan, Hezîran, Tîrmeh, Tebax, Îlon, Cotmeh, Mijdar, Kanûn (lowercase inside sentences is fine, capitalised as in the source style). Buttons and actions are short singular imperatives (Tomar bike, Jê bibe, Dîsa biceribîne, Av bide); titles, tabs, headers and buttons use sentence case (only the first word capitalised), except proper names, Coupley, Premium and AI. Script: standard Hawar Latin alphabet with ç ê î ş û (never x̱, ẍ, Arabic script or Turkish ı/ğ); Turkish loanwords only when they are the everyday Kurmanji word (sohbet, belaş). Plural categories are one and other: “%lld roj” is used for both since Kurmanji nouns stay singular after numbers, but keep both forms filled (one: “%lld roj”, other: “%lld roj”). Tone warm, light and kind, never cheesy.",
